WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.167
-Great to see you in person.

00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:03.334
-Oh, it's so good
to see you again, yeah.

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:04.834
-It's great to be here.
You're here.

00:00:04.834 --> 00:00:05.968
You're in New York City.

00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:07.501
You got a live crowd right here.
-Yeah.

00:00:07.501 --> 00:00:10.968
It's so good
to have people back, right?

00:00:10.968 --> 00:00:12.701
-Do you love New York City
when you come visit?

00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:14.267
-Love it.
Absolutely enjoy coming back.

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:15.701
Have such a blast here.
-Yeah.

00:00:15.701 --> 00:00:17.901
Did you ever spend
a lot of time here or no?

00:00:17.901 --> 00:00:20.100
-I -- I first came here
when I was 18.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:24.000
I was traveling
around America by bus.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.200
And I -- first time
I got to New York,

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.334
I had like $50 left.
I had, like, zero money,

00:00:28.334 --> 00:00:30.167
and I was like,
"What am I gonna do?"

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:32.133
So, I thought the last thing
I can do with that money is

00:00:32.133 --> 00:00:34.100
go up -- go up the Eiffel Tower.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.267
-Oh, the Empire --

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:37.300
-No, not the Eiffel Tower.
That's in Paris.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.467
[ Laughter ]
The Empire State Building.

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:40.701
-50 bucks --
-Just testing you guys there.

00:00:40.701 --> 00:00:42.767
-50 bucks, JetBlue
can get you there.

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:44.434
I mean...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.434 --> 00:00:46.801
Yeah, but then you got to pay --
then you got to pay for it,

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:48.033
then go up.
Yeah.

00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:49.734
-And then,
so I got to the top of

00:00:49.734 --> 00:00:51.133
the Empire State Building,
right?

00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:53.367
Getting it right.
-So you had 50 bucks.

00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:55.000
You go, "I'm gonna go..."
-Nothing left.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.467
And I thought...
-Get a cab, go do it.

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:58.634
-Go check it out.
I go to the top,

00:00:58.634 --> 00:01:00.701
I saw Val Kilmer up there.

00:01:00.701 --> 00:01:01.901
Like,
"What's he doing up there?"

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:03.300
I just thought,
"This is -- This is crazy."

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.968
So, Val Kilmer was on top
of the Empire State Building.

00:01:05.968 --> 00:01:07.534
-By himself?
-Yeah.

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:08.968
Not quite sure what he was
doing, up there, but I mean --

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.200
-Wow!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.901
What was he -- was he just
enjoying the views?

00:01:11.901 --> 00:01:13.367
-I think he was.
I should have spoken to him.

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:14.400
I should've said something.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:15.467
-You didn't say anything
to Val Kilmer?

00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:16.934
-Oh, no, no.
Or bought him a hot dog

00:01:16.934 --> 00:01:17.934
or something, I don't know.

00:01:17.934 --> 00:01:19.434
-He's a --
He's the funniest guy.

00:01:19.434 --> 00:01:22.534
He's the nicest guy.
He's Batman.

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:25.067
-He is Batman, right.
-Yes, he was Batman, yeah.

00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:28.300
-Certainly a lot better than
the Batmans we saw before.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.934
-Well, yeah --
-I mean, they were good --

00:01:30.934 --> 00:01:32.968
-But you have a little history
of being Batman.

00:01:32.968 --> 00:01:34.100
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:35.701
-You were in a show called
"Batman Live."

00:01:35.701 --> 00:01:37.901
-That's right, yeah.
A couple years ago, I --

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:40.000
-This is Sam in --
-Geez.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.901
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:46.167
-Now, what --
What was "Batman Live"?

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:48.067
Was it -- Was it a musical?
-That was --

00:01:48.067 --> 00:01:52.567
It's a -- It's a stage show.
It's like a Cirque show.

00:01:52.567 --> 00:01:53.667
And we went
all around the world.

00:01:53.667 --> 00:01:56.367
We kinda --
We did the Staples Center,

00:01:56.367 --> 00:01:59.234
we did Vegas, we did
all around the world, yeah.

00:01:59.234 --> 00:02:01.767
-This is before
"Outlander," obviously.

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:05.100
-Before, yeah, yeah, yeah.
-I mean, can we -- can we --

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:07.834
-I'm not sure if Batman's
ever worn a kilt, has he?

00:02:07.834 --> 00:02:10.367
Probably a bit weird, right?
-No, yeah, you never know.

00:02:10.367 --> 00:02:11.601
Probably be --
But it'd be interesting.

00:02:11.601 --> 00:02:13.334
A Batman in a kilt, I would do.
-Right.

00:02:13.334 --> 00:02:15.434
-Would you ever do a Batman,
if they asked you to do --

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:16.868
-Oh, my God.
-You have the jaw line.

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:18.000
-I mean --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.834
Thank you very much.
I mean your jaw's --

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:21.667
Oh, yes, come on.
-This is --

00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:23.334
-Wow, all right.
-This is real.

00:02:23.334 --> 00:02:24.801
-Do I get to do it?
-Yeah.

00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:28.367
-All right.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:30.334
Where am I looking?
-Look over at 1.

00:02:30.334 --> 00:02:32.400
-Oh, I got it,
I got it, I got it.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.200
[ Dark music plays ]

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:35.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.901 --> 00:02:38.267
-Where did that music come from?
Okay, okay.

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:40.400
[ Clears throat ]

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.200
"I am Batman."

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:43.734
-Wow!
That's actually fantastic!

00:02:43.734 --> 00:02:47.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.467
I --
[ Dark music plays ]

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:49.501
[ Chuckles ]

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:51.567
[ Laughter ]
-"I need a sidekick."

00:02:51.567 --> 00:02:53.200
-What?
-"I need a sidekick."

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:55.334
-"Do you need one that looks
and talks just like you?"

00:02:55.334 --> 00:02:57.667
-"Yeah."
-"Then I'm right here."

00:02:57.667 --> 00:02:59.267
-"There you are."
-"I'm Batman."

00:02:59.267 --> 00:03:01.801
-"Ah, I'm Batman."
-"Cool."

00:03:01.801 --> 00:03:03.033
[ Applause ]

00:03:03.033 --> 00:03:04.367
-Dude, Batman and Batman,
would be --

00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:06.701
that would be the next --
-That's the next movie, right?

00:03:06.701 --> 00:03:09.701
-Before we get into "Outlander,"
I want to congratulate you.

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:11.267
Before,
we've talked about your whiskey.

00:03:11.267 --> 00:03:13.534
This is a sassenach?
-Yes.

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:14.767
-Is how you pronounce it.
-That's right.

00:03:14.767 --> 00:03:16.267
-Thank you.
And, congrats,

00:03:16.267 --> 00:03:19.534
'cause you made this whiskey,
and you're Scottish, and you go,

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:20.667
"Yeah, I'm gonna
make a whiskey,"

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:21.868
and you don't mess around.
-Right, right.

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.467
-You ended up winning
all these awards for it.

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:25.300
I go, "That's fantastic.
Congratulations."

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.567
And it's all awesome.

00:03:26.567 --> 00:03:28.100
Then you show up today.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.601
I go, "Good to see you, Sam.
What's up?"

00:03:29.601 --> 00:03:32.601
You go, "Got a present for you."
And I go, "Whiskey."

00:03:32.601 --> 00:03:34.801
And I look and it's not.
It's tequila.

00:03:34.801 --> 00:03:36.133
-Right. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:38.000
-Now I go, "Well, maybe he
thinks I have a problem."

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:39.434
-Yeah, I just keep
bringing you alcohol.

00:03:39.434 --> 00:03:41.667
-Keep bringing me alcohol,
I go, "Oh, thank you, tequila."

00:03:41.667 --> 00:03:43.267
And you go,
"Yeah, but it's my tequila."

00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:45.100
-Yeah.
-You're in the tequila business.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.567
-We are, yeah, yeah.
Randomly went to --

00:03:47.567 --> 00:03:49.567
to Mexico to just go
to the highlands there,

00:03:49.567 --> 00:03:52.834
and just met these guys
at El Tequileno,

00:03:52.834 --> 00:03:54.501
and they are just
master distillers.

00:03:54.501 --> 00:03:56.968
They are Mexico's
best-kept secret.

00:03:56.968 --> 00:03:59.100
They're the most popular
blanco in tequila.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:00.868
And we just realized --
we bonded.

00:04:00.868 --> 00:04:02.467
Like, they love good spirits.

00:04:02.467 --> 00:04:04.167
I'm Scottish,
we love good spirits.

00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:05.634
-Yeah.
-And the stories are the same,

00:04:05.634 --> 00:04:07.567
the culture,
and we decided to collaborate,

00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:08.934
and make this amazing tequila.

00:04:08.934 --> 00:04:10.367
-And then you made
this amazing tequila.

00:04:10.367 --> 00:04:11.934
What is it called?
-It's called

00:04:11.934 --> 00:04:14.000
the Sassenach Select:
El Tequileno,"

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:16.067
and we just won a couple of
gold medals for it, as well.

00:04:16.067 --> 00:04:18.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Another award winning --

00:04:18.801 --> 00:04:20.334
I mean, dude, you --
-What's next, right?

00:04:20.334 --> 00:04:21.367
-I'm so happy.
That's so cool.

00:04:21.367 --> 00:04:22.400
-What do you want?
We'll make it.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:23.968
-Yeah, what do you --
I like gin,

00:04:23.968 --> 00:04:26.000
if you want to work on a gin.
-Oh, we could do that, yeah.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:27.868
Jimmy's Gin?
-Ginny Fallon.

00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:29.968
Yeah, go for it, you take it.
-Ginny Fallon.

00:04:29.968 --> 00:04:32.000
-Take the name.
Let's talk "Outlander."

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.300
-Okay, yes.
-Okay.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:36.400
Season six returns on Sunday.
People cannot wait.

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:38.200
In fact, people --
when you're off,

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:39.868
they call it
"The Droughtlander."

00:04:39.868 --> 00:04:41.133
-"Droughtlander," yeah, yeah.

00:04:41.133 --> 00:04:42.801
-Yeah,
they really miss the show.

00:04:42.801 --> 00:04:45.200
-Each year, the Droughtlander
gets slightly longer.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:48.801
This year, the break has been
almost two years

00:04:48.801 --> 00:04:49.834
between seasons, so --

00:04:49.834 --> 00:04:51.100
I think we're just
testing our fans.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:52.367
Like, next time,
it will be like a decade.

00:04:52.367 --> 00:04:53.534
-No, you can't do that.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:55.934
-Just, like, pushing them.
-But, you know,

00:04:55.934 --> 00:04:58.968
it's based off some amazing
books, amazing writing.

00:04:58.968 --> 00:05:01.901
But the author's
only working on her --

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:04.033
-Diana Gabaldon --
And thank you, Diana.

00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:05.567
She's -- She has written
this amazing series.

00:05:05.567 --> 00:05:07.901
She's on book 10.
We're on book --

00:05:07.901 --> 00:05:10.367
We're about to do book seven
in season seven,

00:05:10.367 --> 00:05:12.100
so we've still got
a bit of way to go.

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:14.734
-Do you know how it ends?
-I do.

00:05:14.734 --> 00:05:16.133
I do.
I know how it ends.

00:05:16.133 --> 00:05:17.767
-See, I don't know if you're
lying to me or if you're acting.

00:05:17.767 --> 00:05:19.133
-Ah, yeah.
-Wow, you're really --

00:05:19.133 --> 00:05:20.734
-Yeah, no.
-You're in your Batman role

00:05:20.734 --> 00:05:22.934
right now. I like it.
-Yeah.

00:05:22.934 --> 00:05:24.868
She -- "I'm Batman."
No, she revealed to me --

00:05:24.868 --> 00:05:28.567
she revealed to me the ending
a long time ago, actually, so...

00:05:28.567 --> 00:05:30.000
-She's written the end
but she hasn't written --

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.267
-Yeah, yeah.
-It's in her head?

00:05:31.267 --> 00:05:32.434
She knows how it ends?
-In her head

00:05:32.434 --> 00:05:34.734
and in my e-mail chain, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:36.534
-Oh, my God.
-Let's hope I don't get hacked.

00:05:36.534 --> 00:05:39.067
-Yeah, I know,
I hope you don't -- oh, my gosh.

00:05:39.067 --> 00:05:41.167
"I'm Batman" is your password.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.167 --> 00:05:43.501
-How did you know?
Oh.

00:05:43.501 --> 00:05:45.100
-But that's wild.
All right, so what --

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:46.868
How can you set up
the new season for everybody?

00:05:46.868 --> 00:05:50.400
-So, we're picking up
a short time after the end

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:54.701
of season five,
and Claire was assaulted.

00:05:54.701 --> 00:05:56.901
She's kind of suffering
a lot of trauma from that.

00:05:56.901 --> 00:05:59.267
We have the War of Independence
fast approaching,

00:05:59.267 --> 00:06:01.801
and then, my character
meets an old adversary

00:06:01.801 --> 00:06:03.000
in the form of Tom Christie,

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:05.334
so there's so many things
happening this season.

00:06:05.334 --> 00:06:08.167
It's a shorter season, but some
of the episodes are much longer.

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:10.667
So it --
it really is very intense.

00:06:10.667 --> 00:06:12.434
-Guys, get ready.
I want to show a clip.

00:06:12.434 --> 00:06:15.234
Here's Sam Heughan in season 6
premiere of "Outlander."

00:06:15.234 --> 00:06:16.534
Take a look.

00:06:16.534 --> 00:06:19.901
-Tom received word
his wife had died

00:06:19.901 --> 00:06:21.534
while we were Ardsmuir.

00:06:21.534 --> 00:06:24.868
But you?

00:06:24.868 --> 00:06:28.667
You were there with me,
in the prison.

00:06:28.667 --> 00:06:30.334
I saw you.

00:06:30.334 --> 00:06:33.033
♪♪

00:06:33.033 --> 00:06:36.701
It's what got me through it.

00:06:36.701 --> 00:06:38.567
You are always with me.

00:06:38.567 --> 00:06:42.200
♪♪

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:45.334
Sometimes, I...

00:06:45.334 --> 00:06:48.300
I think you're an angel, Claire.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:56.534
♪♪

00:06:56.534 --> 00:06:59.400
-Come on.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:00.534
Come on.

00:07:00.534 --> 00:07:02.834
Sam Heughan right there,
everybody.

00:07:02.834 --> 00:07:06.467
Season six of "Outlander"
premieres this Sunday on Starz,

00:07:06.467 --> 00:07:07.968
and we're working
on our Batman movie.

00:07:07.968 --> 00:07:08.968
We are.

